[01:53.84] Now in this far away land
[02:00.01] Strange that the palms of my hands
[02:05.49] Should be damp with expectancy
[03:25.55] Spring, and the air's turning mild
[03:31.82] City lights and the glimpse of a child
[03:37.22] Of the alleyway infantry
[03:44.94] Friends, do they know what I mean?
[03:51.18] Rain and the gathering green
[03:56.44] Of an afternoon out of town
[04:05.38] But Lord I had to go
[04:08.24] The trail was laid too slow behind me
[04:14.14] To face the call of fame
[04:16.89] Or make a drunkard's name for me
[04:21.69] Though now this better life
[04:24.25] Has brought a different understanding
[04:29.44] And from these endless days
[04:31.71] Shall come a broader sympathy
[04:37.83] And though I count the hours
[04:41.46] To be alone's no injury
[04:46.95] My home was a place by the sand
[04:53.96] Cliffs and a military band
[04:59.00] Blew an air of normality
[05:00.46] 